// @consolidated-test (generated by consolidate_tests.py)
/*
 * mso_validation_test.cj
 *
 * Unit tests for mdsec_issuer_auth feature — fc_mdsec_issuer_auth:
 *
 * done_when 1: validateDigestValues — MSO ValueDigests vs actual IssuerSignedItem digest
 *   - positive case: correct digest → no error
 *   - negative case: tampered item bytes → invalidDigestValues error
 *
 * done_when 2: validateValidityInfo + digestAlgorithm support
 *   - validity expired → validityInfoError
 *   - unsupported algorithm → unsupportedDigestAlgorithm error
 *
 * done_when 3: MSO issuer certificate chain via x509.verifyChain
 *   - positive case: no x5chain → signatureVerificationFailed / issuerTrustFailed
 *
 * Note on cert chain positive test: full verifyChain with real DER certs requires
 * an actual CA/leaf cert pair, which is not available in unit test context.
 * The test verifies the correct error path (empty chain) and a successful parse
 * path (single self-signed DER fixture that fails chain but confirms parse).
 * The integration test (done_when 3) coverage is documented in Hand-off.
 */
